Chapter: RocRecArithEval
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_recursive_data_tests.zig,
 "inspect: recursive nominal arithmetic expr":

     Arith := [Lit(I64), Add(Arith, Arith), Mul(Arith, Arith), Neg(Arith)]
     main = Arith.Mul(Arith.Add(Arith.Lit(2), Arith.Lit(3)), Arith.Neg(Arith.Lit(4)))

 Roc inspects the value as `Mul(Add(Lit(2), Lit(3)), Neg(Lit(4)))`. Codex has
 no inspect, so the port writes the printer by hand and ALSO evaluates the
 tree, which Roc's case does not: a second line, -20, that a wrong
 constructor order could not fake.

Section: Types

  Arith =
   | Lit (Integer)
   | Add (Arith) (Arith)
   | Mul (Arith) (Arith)
   | Neg (Arith)

Section: Functions

  arith-text : Arith -> Text
  arith-text (e) =
   when e
    is Lit (n) -> "Lit(" & show n & ")"
    is Add (a) (b) -> "Add(" & arith-text a & ", " & arith-text b & ")"
    is Mul (a) (b) -> "Mul(" & arith-text a & ", " & arith-text b & ")"
    is Neg (a) -> "Neg(" & arith-text a & ")"

  arith-eval : Arith -> Integer
  arith-eval (e) =
   when e
    is Lit (n) -> n
    is Add (a) (b) -> arith-eval a + arith-eval b
    is Mul (a) (b) -> arith-eval a * arith-eval b
    is Neg (a) -> 0 - arith-eval a

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   let tree = Mul (Add (Lit 2) (Lit 3)) (Neg (Lit 4))
   in act
    print-line-uni (arith-text tree)
    print-line-uni (show (arith-eval tree))
   end
  end
